# Webhook Example
    This project is a basic implementation of a webhook architecture with two main components: a sender server and a receiver server. The application shows how to log an event on the sending server and send the data to the receiving server through a webhook.

## Technologies Used
    Node.js: Platform for executing JavaScript code on the server.
    Express.js: Framework to handle HTTP routes and requests.
    Axios: HTTP client to make requests to the receiving server.
    Postman: Tool to test and simulate HTTP requests.
### Project Structure

    webhook-example/
    ├── receiverWebhook.js.   
    ├── senderWebhook.js    
    ├── package.json       
    └─── README.md          
### Prerequisites.
    Before running the project, make sure you have the following installed:

    Node.js 
    Postman (optional, for testing).
### Installation
    Clone this repository:

    https://github.com/Cristina-Colcha/Ejemplo_Webhook.git 
    cd webhook-example
### Install the dependencies:

    npm install
### Execute
    Start the receiver server:
     node receiverWebhook.js
    This will start the receiver server on port 3000.

    Start the sender server:
     node senderWebhook.js
    This will start the sender server on port 4000.

### Testing
    Open Postman and send a POST request to the sender server endpoint:

    URL: http://localhost:4000/register
    Method: POST
    Body (JSON format):
    json

            {
            “name": ‘Carlos Perez’,
            “email": ‘carlos.perez@example.com’,
            “event": ”new_user”
            }
    In the console of the sender server (senderWebhook.js), you should see that the webhook was sent successfully.
    In the console of the receiving server (receiverWebhook.js), you should see that the data was received and processed.
